# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Verknüpfte QPU-Jobs abbrechen {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Wenn du einen verwalteten Workflow-Job mit `job.cancel()` abbrichst, versucht der Workflow auch, die QPU-Arbeit abzubrechen, die er gestartet hat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Sessions und Batches.** Der Workflow bricht jede seiner Sessions und Batches ab, wodurch auch deren Jobs in der Warteschlange abgebrochen werden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Andere Primitive-Jobs.** Der Workflow bricht jeden seiner anderen Primitive-Jobs ab, die noch in der Warteschlange stehen oder laufen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` gibt für jeden QPU-Job und jede Session eine Meldung zurück, sodass du prüfen kannst, was abgebrochen wurde:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Bei einem Workflow, der in einem Batch lief, sieht die Meldung wie folgt aus:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Wenn der Client aus deinen lokalen Zugangsdaten keinen `QiskitRuntimeService` erstellen kann, bricht er nur den verwalteten Workflow-Job ab. Brich die QPU-Jobs selbst mit ihren IDs aus `job.runtime_jobs()` ab.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Wenn ein Workflow einen Job selbst stoppt, zum Beispiel weil er das 24-Stunden-Limit erreicht hat, bricht er seine QPU-Jobs nicht ab. Brich sie mit ihren IDs aus `job.runtime_jobs()` ab.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "QPU-Jobs in einem Workflow beheben {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problem | Ursache |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` löst `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'` aus. | Der Code läuft in deinem lokalen Notebook, nicht in einem verwalteten Workflow-Job. Verwende lokal `QiskitRuntimeService()`. |\n"
"| `update_status()` gibt `False` zurück, und die Logs zeigen `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Der Wert ist keine der `Job`-Konstanten, oder der Job ist nicht mehr aktiv. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` gibt `[]` zurück. | Der Workflow hat seinen Service mit `QiskitRuntimeService()` erstellt, oder er hat noch kein Primitive ausgeführt. |\n"
"| Die Jobs einer Session werden nicht nachverfolgt. | Die Session wurde aus einem Backend eines anderen Service erstellt. Hole das Backend aus `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| Die Workflow-Logs zeigen `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Der Workflow konnte einen Primitive-Job nicht aufzeichnen. Der Primitive-Job läuft trotzdem, wird aber nicht nachverfolgt. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` zeigt `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Der Client konnte aus deinen lokalen Zugangsdaten keinen `QiskitRuntimeService` erstellen und hat daher nur den verwalteten Workflow-Job abgebrochen. |\n"
"| `client.job()` schlägt mit `Job [...] not found` fehl. | Die Job-ID ist falsch, oder der Job gehört einem anderen Benutzer. |\n"

